    ("heavenly-treasures.md",
     "Jesus commands his followers to lay up treasures in heaven but never lists what they are — this article fills that gap with a twelve-item inventory derived from decades of searching Scripture, starting with the Fear of the Lord and culminating in the Glory of God. The list is organized into a four-category framework — Being (eternal life), Establishing (family, work, authority), Nurturing (love, wisdom, courage), and Flourishing (freedom, happiness, joy) — each grounded in specific biblical texts. The article traces back to the author's memorization of the Sermon on the Mount in his early Christian life and the question it raised that launched over a decade of searching: if Jesus says to treasure things in heaven, what exactly are those things? The answer is not abstract but deeply practical, defining the goals that should orient every Christian's investment of time, energy, and devotion."),

