    ("identification.md",
     "This article — part of the women's ordination series — explores how the Seven Pillars of Wisdom connect to women's voices through figures like Lady Wisdom, Hannah, the Wife of Noble Character, and the Bride of Song of Songs, building a biblical case for women's full participation in church life. Hannah's prayer is decoded to show seven reversals of fortune matching the seven phases of the Growth Pattern, and her phrase 'the barren has borne seven' is revealed as the earliest prophecy of the seven pillars themselves. The stability phase of the Growth Pattern (1 to 480 AD) is shown to coincide precisely with the historical period when women were progressively removed from church leadership roles — suggesting this was a biblically foretold season of confinement rather than the permanent divine intention. By grounding the discussion in the structural wisdom patterns of the Bible itself, the article argues that Scripture provides its own framework for understanding when and why restrictions on women's ministry were imposed and why they should be lifted."),

